NAME
    dir - list directory contents

SYNOPSIS
    dir [-R] [path | glob]

DESCRIPTION
    Lists a directory. With no argument it lists the current working
    directory; a path lists that directory; a glob (containing * or ?)
    lists the matching entries. Directories are shown with a trailing
    slash. dir is a /bin program.

OPTIONS
    -R    list subdirectories recursively (like tree)

EXAMPLES
    dir              list the current directory
    dir /bin         list a directory by path
    dir *.asm        entries in the CWD matching a glob
    dir /bin/*.bin   glob within another directory
    dir -R /sub      recursive listing of /sub

SEE ALSO
    tree, find, cd, pwd, ls
